  "Question": "When proving that \\(f(x)=x+1\\) is increasing, \\(f(x_2)-f(x_1)\\) equals \\(x_2-x_1\\). If \\(x_2-x_1=5\\), what is this difference?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "5",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The output difference equals \\(x_2-x_1\\), which is positive for every \\(x_1<x_2\\), so the function is increasing. Substituting the given \\(x_2-x_1=5\\), the requested difference is\n\\[\nf(x_2)-f(x_1)=5.\n\\]",
